CLASS com/charlesproxy/gui/utils/UIUtils com/charlesproxy/gui/utils/UIUtils
	COMMENT Look-and-feel and component-styling helpers. Several members are vestigial Quaqua /
	COMMENT JGoodies hooks whose bodies Charles 5 emptied when it moved to violetlib Aqua and
	COMMENT FlatLaf. The obfuscator strips parameters that a body no longer reads, so those show
	COMMENT up as no-arg no-ops whose call sites still evaluate-and-pop the old argument; the
	COMMENT leftover pop is the only surviving evidence of the original descriptor.
	FIELD field_2353 REDO_KEYSTROKE Ljavax/swing/KeyStroke;
		COMMENT Cmd-Shift-Z on macOS, Ctrl-Y elsewhere. Bound to "redo" by installUndoSupport.
	FIELD field_2354 UNDO_KEYSTROKE Ljavax/swing/KeyStroke;
		COMMENT Cmd-Z / Ctrl-Z. Bound to "undo" by installUndoSupport.
	FIELD field_2355 LOGGER Lorg/slf4j/Logger;
	FIELD field_2356 osVersion Lcom/xk72/lib/class_1558;
		COMMENT Compared against "10.11" to decide whether the Helvetica Neue substitution is
		COMMENT needed, so this is the OS version rather than the Java version. The Charles 4
		COMMENT corpus has the same pair of fields on its UIUtils, named javaVersion/osVersion.
	METHOD method_1965 isAquaLookAndFeel ()Z
	METHOD method_1966 displayFontOptionsChanged (Ljava/lang/String;Ljava/lang/Integer;)V
		ARG 0 displayFont
		ARG 1 displayFontSize
	METHOD method_1967 deriveEmptyBorder (Ljava/lang/String;Ljava/lang/String;)V
		COMMENT Replaces the UIDefaults border at targetKey with an EmptyBorder carrying
		COMMENT sourceKey's insets, unconditionally. Contrast deriveEmptyBorderIfAbsent, which
		COMMENT has the same descriptor but only fills targetKey in when it is missing.
		ARG 0 sourceKey
		ARG 1 targetKey
	METHOD method_1968 configureScopeBarTabbedPane (Ljavax/swing/JTabbedPane;)V
		COMMENT Sets "ScopeBar.tabStyle" to "attached" plus the Quaqua visual-margin properties,
		COMMENT i.e. the tab bar drawn by gui/laf/ScopeBarTabbedPaneUI. Used for the transaction
		COMMENT viewer and chart panel tab bars.
		ARG 0 tabbedPane
	METHOD method_1969 installUndoSupport (Ljavax/swing/text/JTextComponent;)V
		COMMENT Attaches an UndoManager as the "com.charlesproxy.UndoManager" client property,
		COMMENT registers it as an UndoableEditListener, and binds UNDO_KEYSTROKE/REDO_KEYSTROKE.
		ARG 0 textComponent
	METHOD method_1970 maybeConfigureMenuBar ()V
		COMMENT [inferred] Empty no-op. Its one call site is immediately after `new JMenuBar()` in
		COMMENT CharlesFrame and before any menu is added, and the Charles 4 corpus has an
		COMMENT unnamed (Ljavax/swing/JMenuBar;)V sibling of the JMenu hook below, so the
		COMMENT stripped parameter was almost certainly that JMenuBar. What it used to do is lost.
	METHOD method_1971 maybeEnableLCDTextRendering ()V
		COMMENT [inferred] Empty no-op apart from a `getstatic Boolean.TRUE; pop` — the stripped
		COMMENT argument of a callee that was itself stripped to nothing and inlined. That
		COMMENT constant is exactly the second parameter maybeSetCanRenderLCDText takes, and the
		COMMENT Charles 4 corpus pairs enableLCDTextRendering(JComponent) with
		COMMENT setCanRenderLCDText(JComponent, Boolean). Call sites are freshly built panels,
		COMMENT tabbed panes and text areas, which fits a JComponent parameter.
	METHOD method_1972 maybeDisableMenuIcons ()V
		COMMENT [inferred] Empty no-op called once per menu, between `new XMenu(...)` and
		COMMENT `menuBar.add(...)`, in CharlesFrame and HelpMenu — so the stripped parameter was
		COMMENT the JMenu. The Charles 4 corpus names the same-shaped (Ljavax/swing/JMenu;)V
		COMMENT method setJgoodiesDisableIcons, which would explain the empty body: Charles 5 no
		COMMENT longer ships the JGoodies look and feel. That name is itself inferred, so the
		COMMENT vendor-neutral form is used here.
	METHOD method_1973 getPanelInsets ()Ljava/lang/String;
		COMMENT Returns a MigLayout insets string: "1lp 1lp 2lp 1lp" under Aqua, otherwise the
		COMMENT "panel" keyword. Only used as the "ins " argument of a MigLayout constraint.
	METHOD method_1974 restyleSplitPaneDividerForTheme (Lcom/charlesproxy/gui/laf/MyFlatSplitPaneUI;Ljavax/swing/JSplitPane;Lcom/charlesproxy/gui/utils/class_861;)V
		COMMENT The themeChanged body configureSplitPane registers for its FlatLaf branch: pushes
		COMMENT the current divider colour into the UI delegate and restates the FlatLaf style.
		ARG 0 splitPaneUI
		ARG 1 splitPane
		ARG 2 event
	METHOD method_1975 configureTreeTable (Lcom/charlesproxy/gui/lib/treetable/JTreeTable;)V
		ARG 0 treeTable
	METHOD method_1976 configureTreeTable (Lcom/charlesproxy/gui/lib/treetable/JTreeTable;Ljava/util/EnumSet;)V
		COMMENT Adds NotInset to the caller's options before configuring the embedded tree, then
		COMMENT insets the table itself instead — the tree is inside the table's viewport, so
		COMMENT insetting both would double the margin.
		ARG 0 treeTable
		ARG 1 options
	METHOD method_1977 installLookAndFeelForTheme (Lcom/charlesproxy/gui/utils/class_861;)V
		COMMENT The themeChanged body installLookAndFeel registers with a null component, so it
		COMMENT runs once at startup and again on every appearance change. Picks violetlib Aqua
		COMMENT on macOS and FlatLaf light/dark elsewhere, installs the MigLayout visual paddings
		COMMENT and button order for the chosen LaF, then walks Frame.getFrames() calling
		COMMENT SwingUtilities.updateComponentTreeUI.
		ARG 0 event
	METHOD method_1978 applyAwtFontDesktopHints (Ljava/awt/Graphics2D;)V
		ARG 0 graphics
	METHOD method_1979 maybeGrowFrameBoundsForTitleBar (Ljava/awt/Rectangle;)Ljava/awt/Rectangle;
		COMMENT Under Aqua only, returns the rectangle with its height increased by 22 — the
		COMMENT macOS title-bar height. Applied by CharlesFrame to the main-window bounds read
		COMMENT back from StartupConfiguration, before they are clamped to the screen, so the
		COMMENT stored size is being reinterpreted from content area to outer frame. The "why" is
		COMMENT inferred from that one call site; the arithmetic is not.
		ARG 0 bounds
	METHOD method_1980 runOnEDT (Ljava/lang/Runnable;)V
		ARG 0 runnable
	METHOD method_1981 substituteSystemFont (Ljava/lang/String;)V
		COMMENT If the UIDefaults font at key is Helvetica Neue, swaps it for ".System.<size>",
		COMMENT but only when that synthetic family actually resolves.
		ARG 0 key
	METHOD method_1982 installLookAndFeel (Ljava/lang/String;Ljava/lang/Integer;)V
		COMMENT Entry point, run on the EDT from Main just before CharlesFrame is constructed.
		COMMENT Registers installLookAndFeelForTheme, then applies the font options.
		ARG 0 displayFont
		ARG 1 displayFontSize
	METHOD method_1983 deriveEmptyBorderIfAbsent (Ljava/lang/String;Ljava/lang/String;)V
		COMMENT Fills targetKey in from sourceKey's insets only when targetKey has no border yet,
		COMMENT mirroring the right inset down to the left one so the result is symmetric.
		COMMENT Contrast deriveEmptyBorder, same descriptor, which always overwrites.
		ARG 0 sourceKey
		ARG 1 targetKey
	METHOD method_1984 configureCheckBox (Ljavax/swing/JCheckBox;)V
		COMMENT Windows only: clears opacity and tracks the theme background. A no-op elsewhere.
		ARG 0 checkBox
	METHOD method_1985 isFrameActive (Ljavax/swing/JComponent;)Z
		COMMENT True unless the component carries "Frame.active" set to FALSE, and true for null.
		COMMENT The Charles 4 corpus names its same-descriptor counterpart isComponentInactive,
		COMMENT i.e. the opposite polarity; the body here reads as "active", and that legacy name
		COMMENT is itself inferred, so it is not followed.
		ARG 0 component
	METHOD method_1986 configureGroupBox (Ljavax/swing/JPanel;Ljava/lang/String;)V
		ARG 0 panel
		ARG 1 title
	METHOD method_1987 configureScrollPane (Ljavax/swing/JScrollPane;)V
		COMMENT Empty border, and both the pane and its viewport non-opaque. The Charles 4 corpus
		COMMENT calls the same-descriptor method useEmptyBorder.
		ARG 0 scrollPane
	METHOD method_1988 configureSplitPane (Ljavax/swing/JSplitPane;)V
		COMMENT Thin divider: a client property under Aqua, an explicit size of 1 otherwise, plus
		COMMENT a MyFlatSplitPaneUI installed under FlatLaf. The Charles 4 corpus calls the
		COMMENT same-descriptor method setupDividerSizes.
		ARG 0 splitPane
	METHOD method_1989 maybeConfigureTabbedPane (Ljavax/swing/JTabbedPane;)V
		COMMENT [inferred] Body is only setOpaque(false), identical to
		COMMENT maybeConfigureFramesTabbedPane; the two are told apart solely by their call
		COMMENT sites, and they need distinct names because they share a descriptor. This one is
		COMMENT the general case — the breakpoints dialog and AbstractTabbedModelViewFrame.
		ARG 0 tabbedPane
	METHOD method_1990 fillViewportHeightWith (Ljavax/swing/JTable;)V
		ARG 0 table
	METHOD method_1991 configureTextField (Ljavax/swing/JTextField;)V
		COMMENT Undo support only. Widely used across the tool settings panels.
		ARG 0 textField
	METHOD method_1992 configureTitleToolBar (Ljavax/swing/JToolBar;)V
		COMMENT Sets "Quaqua.ToolBar.style" to "title" and, under FlatLaf, a BottomLineBorder
		COMMENT tracking the theme.
		ARG 0 toolBar
	METHOD method_1993 restyleToolBarBorderForTheme (Ljavax/swing/JToolBar;Lcom/charlesproxy/gui/utils/class_861;)V
		COMMENT The themeChanged body configureTitleToolBar registers under FlatLaf: rebuilds the
		COMMENT BottomLineBorder in the new theme's colour.
		ARG 0 toolBar
		ARG 1 event
	METHOD method_1994 configureTree (Ljavax/swing/JTree;)V
		ARG 0 tree
	METHOD method_1995 configureTree (Ljavax/swing/JTree;Ljava/util/EnumSet;)V
		COMMENT Row height is always raised to the font height plus 6; CustomFont additionally
		COMMENT swaps in the configured display font, and NotInset suppresses the inset viewStyle.
		ARG 0 tree
		ARG 1 options
	METHOD method_1996 configureTextArea (Ljavax/swing/text/JTextComponent;)V
		ARG 0 textComponent
	METHOD method_1997 configureTextArea (Ljavax/swing/text/JTextComponent;Z)V
		COMMENT The flag selects the monospaced derivation of the configured display font over
		COMMENT the plain one; callers that pass true are the log, EULA and raw-body views.
		ARG 0 textComponent
		ARG 1 monospace
	METHOD method_1998 isFlatLaf ()Z
	METHOD method_1999 maybeConfigureFramesTabbedPane (Ljavax/swing/JTabbedPane;)V
		COMMENT [inferred] Body is only setOpaque(false), identical to maybeConfigureTabbedPane.
		COMMENT Its one call site is TabbedDesktopPane's own tab strip — the window tabs drawn by
		COMMENT gui/laf/FramesTabbedPaneUI — which is where the "Frames" in the name comes from.
		ARG 0 tabbedPane
	METHOD method_2000 getAwtFontDesktopHints ()Ljava/util/Map;
		COMMENT The "awt.font.desktophints" desktop property, i.e. the platform's text
		COMMENT antialiasing RenderingHints. Same name in the Charles 4 corpus.
	METHOD method_2001 maybeSetCanRenderLCDText ()V
		COMMENT [inferred] Empty no-op. Its one call site, StatusPanelLabel.setEtched, still
		COMMENT evaluates `Boolean.valueOf(this.lozenge)` and pops it, so a Boolean parameter was
		COMMENT stripped; the receiver-shaped `aload_0` beside it would have been dropped without
		COMMENT trace. That gives (JComponent, Boolean), which is the descriptor the Charles 4
		COMMENT corpus has for setCanRenderLCDText. macOS-only, and paired with
		COMMENT maybeEnableLCDTextRendering, whose vestigial Boolean.TRUE is this parameter.
	METHOD method_2002 substituteSystemFonts ()V
		COMMENT Runs substituteSystemFont over every UIDefaults key ending in "font" or "Font".
		COMMENT Only reached under Aqua on macOS 10.11 and later.
	METHOD method_4327 isWhitespaceOrPeriod (C)Z
	METHOD method_4328 nextWordBoundary (Ljava/lang/String;I)I
		COMMENT Treats '.' as a word separator so caret-next-word steps between the labels of a
		COMMENT hostname. Used by HostnameWordAction.
		ARG 0 text
		ARG 1 offset
	METHOD method_4329 previousWordBoundary (Ljava/lang/String;I)I
		COMMENT The backwards counterpart of nextWordBoundary.
		ARG 0 text
		ARG 1 offset
	METHOD method_4330 configureHostnameTextField (Ljavax/swing/JTextField;)V
		COMMENT configureTextField plus the four HostnameWordAction bindings. Callers are the
		COMMENT external proxy host, external DNS resolver address and location host fields.
		ARG 0 textField
	CLASS HostnameWordAction HostnameWordAction
		FIELD forward forward Z
		FIELD select select Z
	CLASS TreeOptions TreeOptions
		COMMENT Enum constant names are exact: the obfuscator leaves the Enum.name() string in
		COMMENT <clinit>, as the first ldc of the group ending in each putstatic.
		FIELD field_2357 NotInset Lcom/charlesproxy/gui/utils/UIUtils$TreeOptions;
		FIELD field_2358 CustomFont Lcom/charlesproxy/gui/utils/UIUtils$TreeOptions;
		FIELD field_2359 ContentTextSize Lcom/charlesproxy/gui/utils/UIUtils$TreeOptions;
		FIELD field_2360 $VALUES [Lcom/charlesproxy/gui/utils/UIUtils$TreeOptions;
			COMMENT javac's synthetic constant array behind values().
